course: dictionary
lesson: 7415
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. «Polar» is one of them, and the sentence around it tells you which meaning to use. Look for clues such as the other words and the subject being talked about.
explain: «Some polar bears now have to swim much longer distances, sometimes for days.» Polar bears live in the icy Arctic, near the North Pole, so polar here means to do with the very cold areas around a pole. The clue is the bears, the ice and the cold.
explain: Polar can also mean completely opposite. In «polar opposites», the two things are as far apart as they can be, like two ends of a line. The phrase tells you the meaning, not the word on its own.
explain: Always check by putting your meaning into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning of polar.
fact: Polar means to do with the North Pole, the South Pole, or the very cold areas around them.
fact: «Polar opposites» means two things that are completely opposite.
fact: In science, polar means to do with the poles of a magnet or of the Earth.
fact: The polar regions are the Arctic around the North Pole and the Antarctic around the South Pole.
fact: Polar is an adjective with no comparative, so you cannot say more polar.
exercise: «Some polar bears now have to swim much longer distances.» What does polar mean in «polar bears»? | Completely opposite | To do with a magnet | *To do with the very cold areas around the North Pole | Very slow
exercise: Ben says «polar opposites» means two things that are a bit alike. What is the right meaning? | Two things that are very small | Two things that live in the same place | Two things that are made of ice | *Two things that are as different as they can be
exercise: In science, what does polar mean? | *To do with the poles of a magnet or of the Earth | Made of ice only | To do with the sea | Very hot
test: What does polar mean in «polar ice caps»? | A type of hair | Completely opposite | *The very cold areas around a pole | Warm and sunny
test: Ahmed says polar is an adjective, so it can be more polar. Is he right? | *No, polar has no comparative, so it cannot be more polar | Yes, polar, more polar, most polar | Yes, it is more polar than cold
exam: Lena reads «The polar night lasts for weeks.» What does polar mean here? | Completely opposite | Very quiet | To do with a magnet | *To do with the cold areas around the North or South Pole
